    native_build_step5_serial_threads_ignored_2026-09-04, 0, audit=triage-20261027-v4 assessed_sha=c0b3ad911f4cb00c0f3550b05baa8d06347d17d0 review=accepted inspection=source_reviewed validity=valid reproducibility=untested scope=UNRUN solution=known structural=yes action=fix_candidate review_receipt=scoped_v3_aggregate evidence=doc/08_tracking/bug/triage_20261027/reviewed_categories_v4.sdn evidence_sha256=f47867ce23862fe32ca679bd72a0f53a2ea1e0727044f8c32f71209653d4da42 manifest_sha256=20c9585305077f9cdec78d82dee9f3add8fb1d98258b9209ad6169097072296c evidence_commit=b078b2807cf4379640f832a29672119f57e565ff scope_evidence=none scope_sha256=none record_sha256=e84ff97313e089215179e589599511d6dfebb0d480ec9b9569b159b58302c9b1
    native_build_step5_serial_threads_ignored_2026-09-04, 1, "2026-11-03 ROOT CAUSE (conc, origin/release/1.0.0): the only caller of ParallelBuilder is src/compiler/80.driver/driver_aot_native_output.spl:2750 `builder.build(_compile_frozen_module_capsule_prefetched_v1(...))`; it never calls set_spawn_dispatch, so build() (src/compiler/80.driver/driver_build/parallel.spl:442, chunk loops at :587 and :593) runs compile_fn once per unit in-process, no thread, no spawn; --threads N only moves the chunk size. build_parallel() (:635) and build_supervised() (:816) do real rt_process_spawn_async dispatch but have zero callers. Why: compile_fn closes over in-memory frozen MIR capsules (whole-program MIR from step 4) which cannot cross a process boundary. Already parallel: _driver_codegen_pool_prefetch_v1 (driver_aot_native_output.spl:4613, called at :2730) runs llc in N child processes. Still serial in the parent: MIR to LLVM-IR translation of every module and step-4 MIR lowering of the whole program (driver_pipeline_lowering.spl:262-311). Net: phase-3 codegen is bounded by one core of translation. Duplicates folded in: stage3_native_build_serial_ignores_jobs_2026-09-14, item5_native_build_threads_ineffective_2026_10_14."
    native_build_step5_serial_threads_ignored_2026-09-04, 2, "2026-11-03 plan, cost and risk (conc). Per-file child plan: (1) add a per-file child entry `simple compile-unit <file> --target T --out X.o` running parse, HIR, MIR, obj for one file in one process (cc1 style, one-process-per-file); imports come from interface digests (action_key.spl interface_digest_of, or SIF/TLDR), not the parent in-memory MIR. (2) replace in-process build(compile_fn) with set_spawn_dispatch(spawn_fn, collect_fn): spawn_fn launches the child per file, collect_fn admits the .o plus receipt; build_parallel/build_supervised already exist with scheduling tests. (3) worker count from host.sdn (80 threads here) capped by memory budget (per-child RSS times N, at most 64 GB). (4) step-4 whole-program MIR lowering leaves the parent; generics are erased (no mono pass) so no cross-file instantiation pass is needed, which is also the prerequisite. COST: large, about 1-2 weeks; needs the child CLI entry, interface loading without parsing dependency bodies (SIF reader exists, wiring partial), and a stage3 redeploy to verify. RISK: cross-file inlining and const propagation that rely on whole-program MIR; per-child startup (target first object within 10 s); memory N times per-file peak; receipt and determinism parity versus serial output. Cheap interim (medium, verification-pending on stage3): move MIR to IR translation into the existing codegen-pool children by shipping a serialized per-module MIR capsule (needs a capsule serializer). Not implemented in this lane; status kept open."

bug_fix_strategies |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_build_step5_serial_threads_ignored_2026-09-04, 0, "Preferred: per-file child process. Add `simple compile-unit <file> --target T --out X.o` (parse, HIR, MIR, obj in one process), load imports via interface digests (interface_digest_of / SIF) instead of in-memory MIR, and replace builder.build(compile_fn) at driver_aot_native_output.spl:2750 with set_spawn_dispatch(spawn_fn, collect_fn) so the existing build_parallel/build_supervised (parallel.spl:635/:816) run. Workers from host.sdn capped by RSS budget (at most 64 GB). Removes step-4 whole-program MIR lowering from the parent."
    native_build_step5_serial_threads_ignored_2026-09-04, 1, "Cheap interim: move MIR to LLVM-IR translation into the existing llc codegen-pool children (_driver_codegen_pool_prefetch_v1, :4613) by shipping a serialized per-module MIR capsule. Medium effort (needs a capsule serializer); stage3-only verification, so it lands as fix-implemented-verification-pending."
    native_build_step5_serial_threads_ignored_2026-09-04, 2, "Cost and risk: preferred plan about 1-2 weeks; risks are lost cross-file inlining and const-prop, per-child startup (first .o within 10 s), N times per-file peak RSS, receipt and determinism parity with serial output. Verification needs a stage3 redeploy; the perf spec must assert --threads N reaches more than one busy process with explicit wall and RSS budgets."

